1
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:12,263
"The Luckiest Kid in the World."

2
00:00:15,099 --> 00:00:18,853
They say angels have wings and fly.

3
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:25,151
But my angel is always by my side
and never leaves me.

4
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:30,448
She makes sure I'm always full
and delighted.

5
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:36,036
She is the reason
behind my every giggle and smile.

6
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:53,095
My mother never forgets to hug me tightly.

7
00:00:53,179 --> 00:00:56,599
In her arms, I find peace and safety.

8
00:00:57,099 --> 00:00:59,769
And because my mother loves me so much,

9
00:00:59,852 --> 00:01:02,688
there's nothing more
I could ask for in life.

10
00:01:03,439 --> 00:01:08,819
I am the luckiest kid in the world.

11
00:02:43,706 --> 00:02:46,125
-Chairmom! Chairmom!
-Ms. D! Ms. D! Oh--

12
00:02:46,208 --> 00:02:47,835
-Be careful.
-Yes, ma'am.

13
00:02:47,918 --> 00:02:49,128
-Ms. D?
-Yes?

14
00:02:49,211 --> 00:02:50,296
Is it true
that you're making an announcement

15
00:02:50,379 --> 00:02:52,256
at the anniversary celebration
of La Familia?

16
00:02:52,339 --> 00:02:54,633
Any spoilers?

17
00:02:54,717 --> 00:02:56,385
Where did you hear that?

18
00:02:56,468 --> 00:02:58,137
I'm sorry, no spoilers.

19
00:02:58,846 --> 00:03:03,726
Ms. D? Today is the anniversary
of the factory fire, right?

20
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:06,270
What can you say about it?

21
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:08,314
Will today be a celebration

22
00:03:08,397 --> 00:03:11,775
instead of a commemoration of the tragedy?

23
00:03:11,859 --> 00:03:14,236
As the matron of La Familia,

24
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:18,407
I make sure
that we always prioritize the company,

25
00:03:18,741 --> 00:03:21,619
our employees' welfare,

26
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,537
our work ethic,

27
00:03:23,621 --> 00:03:27,958
and most especially, our safety standards.

28
00:03:29,251 --> 00:03:31,253
That's how we commemorate the fire.

29
00:03:31,337 --> 00:03:33,005
We honor it not by forgetting,

30
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:34,340
but by rebuilding and moving forward.

31
00:03:35,257 --> 00:03:37,259
I'll see you later, okay?
Thank you so much.

32
00:03:37,343 --> 00:03:39,261
-Thank you, Ms. D!
-No more questions.

33
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:42,932
A beautiful morning, Ms. D!

34
00:03:43,015 --> 00:03:44,808
As beautiful as the outfit
you're wearing today.

35
00:03:44,892 --> 00:03:45,893
You look very powerful.

36
00:03:45,976 --> 00:03:48,020
-But also very motherly.
-Good morning, Ms. D.

37
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:49,605
Yes. You are radiant.

38
00:03:49,688 --> 00:03:51,482
Oh, enough of the pleasantries.

39
00:03:51,565 --> 00:03:52,858
Is everything ready?

40
00:03:52,942 --> 00:03:54,318
O-Of course, Ms. D.

41
00:03:54,401 --> 00:03:55,444
It's all set.

42
00:03:55,527 --> 00:03:59,114
I can assure you that
everything will go smoothly.

43
00:03:59,198 --> 00:04:01,200
I made sure that
there won't be any problems.

44
00:04:01,283 --> 00:04:03,744
You have nothing to worry about.

45
00:04:03,827 --> 00:04:05,537
Well, there better be none.

46
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:07,122
Yes, yes.

47
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:08,999
-Mm.
-Enzo.

48
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,293
Good morning, Ms. D.

49
00:04:11,377 --> 00:04:12,544
Everyone is waiting.

50
00:04:12,628 --> 00:04:13,754
Okay.

51
00:04:51,917 --> 00:04:52,876
Come here!

52
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:54,753
Stop her!

53
00:05:02,136 --> 00:05:04,304
Stop her!

54
00:05:08,392 --> 00:05:09,643
-My baby!
-Get it!

55
00:05:09,727 --> 00:05:12,104
No! My baby!

56
00:05:13,355 --> 00:05:14,356
Come on!

57
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:15,607
Cut! Cut! Cut!

58
00:05:15,691 --> 00:05:18,152
What the hell? You showed the doll!

59
00:05:18,235 --> 00:05:19,820
You're not supposed to show
that the baby's a doll!

60
00:05:19,903 --> 00:05:21,572
Unbelievable!

61
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:23,657
Excuse me. How'd I do?

62
00:05:23,741 --> 00:05:25,159
I really gave it my all.

63
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:27,411
Huh? Girl, we weren't rolling.

64
00:05:27,494 --> 00:05:29,997
Remember, the director wanted to show

65
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:32,416
Bianca and Daniela
a run-through of the scene.

66
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:35,544
Snap out of it.
This isn't your first time!

67
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:36,628
Director? Hold it.

68
00:05:37,379 --> 00:05:38,547
We're good, Sandy.

69
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:41,425
Daniela, did you see what the woman did?

70
00:05:41,508 --> 00:05:43,552
-Just do exactly what she did.
-Yes, Director.

71
00:05:44,553 --> 00:05:47,639
Bianca, you're doing what Patricia did.

72
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:49,349
Sorry… Sorry, Director.

73
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:51,518
I was texting my manager,

74
00:05:51,602 --> 00:05:53,812
I didn't see it.

75
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:56,982
Sandy, one more time.

76
00:05:57,066 --> 00:05:58,067
From the top.

77
00:05:58,150 --> 00:06:01,779
Tell the stand-ins
to throw in more punches.

78
00:06:02,488 --> 00:06:05,240
And really knock her to the ground.

79
00:06:05,324 --> 00:06:09,661
From the top.
More punches, more violence.

80
00:06:09,745 --> 00:06:12,581
Okay? From the top.
First position, let's go!

81
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:13,707
From the top, ma'am?

82
00:06:13,791 --> 00:06:15,542
Did I stutter? Are you deaf?

83
00:06:15,626 --> 00:06:17,002
-No, ma'am.
-Good. Let's go,

84
00:06:17,086 --> 00:06:18,128
let's go! Reset!

85
00:06:18,212 --> 00:06:19,797
-Sis, you good?
-Reset! First position!

86
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,215
Let's go, let's go!

87
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:23,175
-I'm good.
-From the top!

88
00:06:23,634 --> 00:06:24,760
In five,

89
00:06:24,843 --> 00:06:27,012
four, three…

90
00:06:29,598 --> 00:06:31,183
Good afternoon, everyone.

91
00:06:31,266 --> 00:06:34,520
And welcome to this
very special celebration

92
00:06:34,603 --> 00:06:36,522
for La Familia Corporation.

93
00:06:38,107 --> 00:06:41,902
Today marks another
exciting milestone for La Familia.

94
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:45,280
As we celebrate our 50th anniversary,

95
00:06:45,364 --> 00:06:48,909
we take our biggest step forward yet.

96
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:52,412
And now, please welcome
the woman leading La Familia

97
00:06:52,496 --> 00:06:53,831
into the future.

98
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,749
The Nation's Chairmom,

99
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:57,626
Diana Aragon!

100
00:07:05,425 --> 00:07:07,094
Good afternoon, everyone.

101
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:08,846
Thank you for coming.

102
00:07:08,929 --> 00:07:11,598
For generations,

103
00:07:11,682 --> 00:07:15,769
Cala Soda has been a part
of every Filipino family.

104
00:07:15,853 --> 00:07:17,354
I've always said that

105
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:21,483
we're the silent member
of every Filipino family.

106
00:07:21,567 --> 00:07:25,320
We're there
at every occasion and milestone.

107
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:28,740
Because that is what La Familia
has always been about.

108
00:07:28,824 --> 00:07:31,618
As we celebrate our anniversary

109
00:07:32,286 --> 00:07:35,539
with all of you all over the country,

110
00:07:36,039 --> 00:07:39,209
we've continued our company tradition

111
00:07:39,293 --> 00:07:43,297
of feeding communities across the country.

112
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:47,426
But today, we take our biggest step yet.

113
00:07:48,010 --> 00:07:52,139
We are very proud to announce to you

114
00:07:52,222 --> 00:07:58,103
the partnership between La Familia
and Burger City International.

115
00:07:59,313 --> 00:08:01,940
They will now carry Cala Soda

116
00:08:02,024 --> 00:08:04,818
and the entire line
of La Familia beverages

117
00:08:04,902 --> 00:08:09,615
in their world-famous
fast-food chain branches

118
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:15,579
as La Familia officially expands
across all of the Asia-Pacific region.

119
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:22,085
But that's not
our only surprise today.

120
00:08:22,586 --> 00:08:24,713
I proudly present to you

121
00:08:25,172 --> 00:08:27,257
a new logo

122
00:08:27,341 --> 00:08:32,971
that celebrates the partnership
between La Familia and Burger City.

123
00:09:13,512 --> 00:09:15,889
Oh, my…

124
00:09:17,224 --> 00:09:19,268
Hey, you guys thirsty?

125
00:09:19,351 --> 00:09:20,560
-Hey, bestie.
-I have water and coffee.

126
00:09:20,644 --> 00:09:21,520
Have you sold a lot?

127
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,106
One of them didn't pay.

128
00:09:24,856 --> 00:09:26,149
Are you all thirsty?

129
00:09:26,608 --> 00:09:28,902
Coffee? Water? Anything?

130
00:09:28,986 --> 00:09:30,112
Get your drinks!

131
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:33,073
Director!

132
00:09:33,156 --> 00:09:35,951
Uh… Are you hungry?
I have some fried buns!

133
00:09:36,034 --> 00:09:37,703
It's my specialty.

134
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:39,329
-Look.
-How much?

135
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:40,956
Oh, it's on the house.

136
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:43,333
-Did you put poison in it?
-Of course not!

137
00:09:44,293 --> 00:09:46,336
Mm. It's good.

138
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:47,963
Thanks.

139
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:52,301
Uh… I hope you can
consider me for your next show.

140
00:09:52,384 --> 00:09:54,553
-Mm-hmm.
-But maybe not as a stand-in.

141
00:09:54,636 --> 00:09:56,305
You could throw in some lines for me.

142
00:09:56,388 --> 00:09:58,056
You saw me act earlier, didn't you?

143
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,891
What a suck-up.

144
00:09:59,975 --> 00:10:01,184
She's so annoying.

145
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:03,603
Someone ought to teach her a lesson.

146
00:10:03,937 --> 00:10:05,647
-What do you mean?
-Thank you, sir.

147
00:10:05,731 --> 00:10:06,857
Director!

148
00:10:07,691 --> 00:10:10,319
-Time to pack up.
-Okay. Let's go then.

149
00:10:10,402 --> 00:10:13,280
It's a wrap, talents!
Time to move to the next location.

150
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:14,948
-All right.
-Patricia, where's the scarf?

151
00:10:15,032 --> 00:10:16,408
Oh, here.

152
00:10:16,491 --> 00:10:18,118
Why are you still in costume?

153
00:10:18,201 --> 00:10:19,619
Get changed. We need that costume.

154
00:10:19,703 --> 00:10:20,787
Okay, okay.

155
00:10:20,871 --> 00:10:23,332
-Hand it over afterward.
-Yes.

156
00:10:23,415 --> 00:10:25,042
-Go ahead. I'll follow.
-You sure?

157
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:26,543
-Yes. See you there.
-Okay.

158
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:30,297
Patricia, did they tell you
we're changing locations?

159
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,299
-No. Where's the new location?
-Here.

160
00:10:36,762 --> 00:10:38,680
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

161
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:43,518
You can drop me off here.

162
00:10:45,729 --> 00:10:46,980
Thanks.

163
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:58,575
INDUSTRIA STREET

164
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:05,999
Hello, ma'am?

165
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:09,127
Where are you?
We're about to start rolling!

166
00:11:09,211 --> 00:11:13,256
Yes. I'm already here at Industria Street.

167
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:16,051
What are you doing there?

168
00:11:16,134 --> 00:11:18,595
I was told the location
was changed to here.

169
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:22,015
The location has not been changed!
Oh, my god!

170
00:11:22,099 --> 00:11:24,184
I'll be there. I can still make it, ma'am.

171
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:27,020
Screw this!
Your miscommunication isn't my fault!

172
00:11:27,104 --> 00:11:28,939
I can still make it, ma'am! I'm nearby!

173
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:31,566
Hello? Ma'am? Hello?

174
00:11:43,245 --> 00:11:44,538
What happened?

175
00:11:44,621 --> 00:11:46,164
I'm so sorry, Ms. D.

176
00:11:46,873 --> 00:11:49,668
It was Mabel's responsibility.

177
00:11:49,751 --> 00:11:53,380
She was in charge
of the technical rehearsal.

178
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:58,009
She didn't do her job properly.

179
00:11:58,343 --> 00:11:59,678
Is that so?

180
00:12:00,262 --> 00:12:01,930
Yes, Ms. D.

181
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:05,142
You know what happens to people

182
00:12:05,225 --> 00:12:08,103
who don't live up
to my expectations, don't you?

183
00:12:08,687 --> 00:12:10,605
Of course. Right away.

184
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:17,737
-Mabel.
-Ma'am?

185
00:12:17,821 --> 00:12:20,073
-I'm so sorry. You're fired.
-Huh?

186
00:12:20,407 --> 00:12:21,700
No. Ma'am, please.

187
00:12:21,783 --> 00:12:23,994
There's nothing I can do. Ms. D said so.

188
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:25,787
-So please pack your things.
-Ma'am, please.

189
00:12:25,871 --> 00:12:28,457
Sorry, you're fired. Bye! Bye!

190
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:32,669
I want you to revoke access
for employee #42568.

191
00:12:33,462 --> 00:12:35,464
Escort her out of the building
immediately.

192
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:50,520
-Enzo.
-Uh…

193
00:12:50,604 --> 00:12:51,605
Don't.

194
00:12:56,443 --> 00:12:57,527
She's fired.

195
00:12:58,069 --> 00:12:59,196
Ms. D?

196
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:00,530
Ms. D?

197
00:13:02,073 --> 00:13:04,868
You know why I fired her, don't you?

198
00:13:06,161 --> 00:13:07,370
Yes, Ms. D.

199
00:13:08,205 --> 00:13:10,665
Because this deal is very, very important.

200
00:13:11,666 --> 00:13:12,792
Not just that.

201
00:13:14,169 --> 00:13:18,673
What I hate most is a leader
who cannot take accountability.

202
00:13:18,757 --> 00:13:21,551
Your people's failure is your own failure.

203
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:25,180
And worse, she shifted the blame

204
00:13:25,263 --> 00:13:28,225
for something she was responsible for.

205
00:13:29,184 --> 00:13:31,269
Ms. D? Ms. D?

206
00:13:31,353 --> 00:13:33,313
How long have you been
working for me, Enzo?

207
00:13:33,647 --> 00:13:36,274
Um, it's been seven years.

208
00:13:36,358 --> 00:13:37,692
Since I graduated.

209
00:13:38,068 --> 00:13:40,987
Congratulations.
You're my new Chief of Staff.

210
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:43,573
Let me fix this, Ms. D!

211
00:13:43,657 --> 00:13:45,116
-Let's go.
-No!

212
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,869
No, Ms. D! Don't fire me!

213
00:13:47,953 --> 00:13:50,580
One more chance, Ms. D! Ms. D!

214
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:53,375
Sir, don't do this. Don't do this! Please!

215
00:13:56,169 --> 00:13:57,587
-Bestie.
-Oh, bestie.

216
00:13:58,129 --> 00:13:59,631
What happened? Where were you?

217
00:14:01,091 --> 00:14:04,261
That witch Riza sent me
to the wrong location.

218
00:14:04,344 --> 00:14:06,346
Huh? She was the one who replaced you.

219
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:07,847
Because you weren't here.

220
00:14:07,931 --> 00:14:09,724
Where is she? Where is that witch?

221
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:13,061
Riza! Hey, Riza!

222
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:14,771
Hey! Come out here.

223
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:17,190
Come on! Why'd you do that?
How could you--

224
00:14:17,274 --> 00:14:18,942
Ms. Daniela!
Ms. Bianca! Come to set.

225
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:21,403
-Ms. Daniela! Ms. Bianca!
-Come out, Riza.

226
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:27,867
-Come on. Let's go.
-Bestie, I've got to go.

227
00:14:27,951 --> 00:14:30,120
-I'm in that scene. Okay.
-All right, go ahead.

228
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:35,584
Actors are in, Riza. Come out there.

229
00:14:35,667 --> 00:14:37,168
Talk to me!

230
00:14:39,629 --> 00:14:40,630
You don't want to come out?

231
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,734
Five, four, three, two…

232
00:15:02,068 --> 00:15:04,237
-Action!
-Can I help you?

233
00:15:04,321 --> 00:15:05,739
Excuse me?

234
00:15:06,448 --> 00:15:07,949
How much for the barbecue?

235
00:15:08,867 --> 00:15:09,701
Ten--

236
00:15:22,631 --> 00:15:23,632
Sandy, her reaction.

237
00:15:23,715 --> 00:15:25,634
-Patricia, your line!
-Miss?

238
00:15:25,717 --> 00:15:28,219
-What is going on? Patricia!
-What's the holdup?

239
00:15:28,303 --> 00:15:30,221
We're running out of time!

240
00:15:30,305 --> 00:15:31,681
Come on!

241
00:15:31,765 --> 00:15:34,934
Can we do it or not?

242
00:15:35,018 --> 00:15:37,854
Sorry. I'm so sorry.

243
00:15:39,022 --> 00:15:40,106
Yes. I can do this.

244
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:41,274
-S-Sorry.
-Hey!

245
00:15:41,358 --> 00:15:42,651
-What now?
-I'm supposed to be in the scene.

246
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:43,943
-Can you do it?
-Sorry, I'm late.

247
00:15:44,027 --> 00:15:45,445
You're too late.

248
00:15:45,528 --> 00:15:46,780
From the top.

249
00:15:46,863 --> 00:15:48,281
-Okay, let's go.
-Yes, one more.

250
00:15:48,365 --> 00:15:49,699
-You!
-Hey.

251
00:15:49,783 --> 00:15:51,826
You locked me in the porta potty!

252
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:54,329
-What's going on?
-The nerve of this girl!

253
00:15:54,412 --> 00:15:57,791
You're not fighting fair!
You sent me to the wrong place!

254
00:15:57,874 --> 00:15:59,876
-You want a fair fight?
-Oh!

255
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,544
Come here!

256
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:03,338
Come here!

257
00:16:03,421 --> 00:16:05,215
Stop it! Both of you!

258
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:07,425
Out of my set! Jeez!

259
00:16:07,509 --> 00:16:09,427
Huh? Why am I getting kicked out?

260
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:13,306
I'm just doing my job. You know me.

261
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:15,141
I never cause trouble.

262
00:16:15,225 --> 00:16:17,811
-Director, she started it.
-She provoked me.

263
00:16:18,228 --> 00:16:19,896
-No, she did it.
-Then she's out!

264
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:21,940
For Pete's sake…

265
00:16:22,023 --> 00:16:23,566
Are you okay, Miggy?

266
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:25,402
-Oh, my goodness.
-Again! Again!

267
00:16:25,485 --> 00:16:26,945
-Are you okay? Okay.
-Yes.

268
00:16:27,028 --> 00:16:28,655
-From the top!
-I'm good.

269
00:16:28,738 --> 00:16:30,240
Your line, Patricia.

270
00:16:30,323 --> 00:16:31,533
-Yes, ma'am.
-Okay. Ready?

271
00:16:31,616 --> 00:16:33,993
-Ready. Roll!
-Rolling!

272
00:16:34,077 --> 00:16:36,788
Five, four, three, two…

273
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:38,748
-Action.
-Action!

274
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:41,543
Excuse me, miss.

275
00:16:42,627 --> 00:16:43,962
How much for the barbecue?

276
00:16:46,339 --> 00:16:47,632
Ten pesos!

277
00:16:52,721 --> 00:16:55,056
She told me to fire Mabel. Fire her!

278
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:56,182
And then when I came back--

279
00:16:56,266 --> 00:16:57,809
Ms. D! Ms. D!

280
00:16:57,892 --> 00:16:59,477
-Ms. D! Ms. D!
-Ms. Cynthia. Ms. Cynthia.

281
00:16:59,561 --> 00:17:01,980
Please, hear me out! Ms. D, please!

282
00:17:02,063 --> 00:17:03,189
Let go of me, Enzo!

283
00:17:03,273 --> 00:17:04,274
-Enough.
-Ms. D!

284
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:06,443
It wasn't my fault!

285
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:08,903
The prop malfunctioned!

286
00:17:08,987 --> 00:17:10,196
It was out of my control!

287
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:14,534
Well, that is what happens
when people like you come unprepared.

288
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:17,954
That's it? One mistake?

289
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:21,541
I gave 15 years of my life
working for you!

290
00:17:22,542 --> 00:17:24,335
Ms. D, this is ridiculous!

291
00:17:24,419 --> 00:17:26,588
That one mistake

292
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:30,049
happened on the most important day,

293
00:17:30,133 --> 00:17:33,511
one that would shape La Familia's history
on the global stage.

294
00:17:34,012 --> 00:17:36,264
So don't act like you're some victim,

295
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:38,141
like I did this to you.

296
00:17:38,224 --> 00:17:40,185
You did this to yourself.

297
00:17:40,602 --> 00:17:43,229
This isn't the first time you screwed up.

298
00:17:43,313 --> 00:17:45,732
You've been warned several times.

299
00:17:45,815 --> 00:17:48,651
And that is how accountability works.

300
00:17:49,819 --> 00:17:52,197
That's not accountability!

301
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:53,823
It's cruelty!

302
00:17:53,907 --> 00:17:56,242
No wonder no one loves you!

303
00:17:56,326 --> 00:17:59,329
No wonder your family abandoned you!

304
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,997
This is why you're alone!

305
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:05,877
"Chairmom"? It's all for show!

306
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:08,838
Karma will come back for you!

307
00:18:11,925 --> 00:18:15,303
Karma is no match for Diana Aragon.

308
00:18:24,062 --> 00:18:27,398
You're the devil!
You're the devil! You ruined my life!

309
00:18:27,482 --> 00:18:29,651
You ruined my life!

310
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:32,695
You won't get away with this!
You will pay for this!

311
00:18:34,322 --> 00:18:36,241
You will pay for this!

312
00:18:37,617 --> 00:18:39,494
La Familia!

313
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:57,929
What's… What's that smell?

314
00:18:58,012 --> 00:18:59,931
Did someone cook dried fish?

315
00:19:00,765 --> 00:19:03,017
We cooked it in the back kitchen, Ms. D.

316
00:19:03,101 --> 00:19:04,561
Hours ago.

317
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:11,276
How many times have I said
I don't want to smell dried fish here.

318
00:19:11,359 --> 00:19:14,028
Diana, you look tired.

319
00:19:14,779 --> 00:19:16,614
Come. Chef has cooked dinner.

320
00:19:16,948 --> 00:19:19,284
Nanny, have I not made myself clear?

321
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:21,536
I don't want to smell dried fish here.

322
00:19:21,619 --> 00:19:23,872
Just ignore it. I'll remind them.

323
00:19:23,955 --> 00:19:27,333
It's the anniversary
of your father's death soon.

324
00:19:27,417 --> 00:19:30,461
I've had his mausoleum cleaned,
as you said.

325
00:19:30,962 --> 00:19:32,255
Thank you, Nanny.

326
00:19:33,798 --> 00:19:36,467
I'm sure your father is very proud of you.

327
00:19:37,886 --> 00:19:41,055
La Familia has taken off since…

328
00:19:45,310 --> 00:19:47,103
I'll have your dinner served.

329
00:20:03,119 --> 00:20:04,120
There.

330
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:05,330
-Jeez, Jena.
-Okay, that's good.

331
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:06,956
-Oh! Hey, sis!
-Excuse me.

332
00:20:08,291 --> 00:20:11,294
Hey! Three, four, five,
six, seven, eight!

333
00:20:12,837 --> 00:20:15,298
-Have you cooked rice?
-Oh, no.

334
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:17,216
Hang on, I'm almost done!

335
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:18,760
Wait, I'm just…

336
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:20,261
I'm just wrapping this up. Wait a sec.

337
00:20:21,596 --> 00:20:22,972
Don't bother. I'll do it.

338
00:20:23,056 --> 00:20:24,641
Thank you, big sis!

339
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:32,815
-Wow, you never stop dancing.
-Ma!

340
00:20:32,899 --> 00:20:34,525
Ma.

341
00:20:37,487 --> 00:20:40,573
Uh, Ma… Do you have 250 pesos to spare?

342
00:20:40,657 --> 00:20:43,743
Come on now, Jena.
I just got back from work,

343
00:20:43,826 --> 00:20:45,954
and this is how you welcome me?

344
00:20:46,037 --> 00:20:47,914
I just need it now, Ma…

345
00:20:47,997 --> 00:20:49,248
Why are you telling me now?

346
00:20:49,332 --> 00:20:52,418
You know my next paycheck's
still a long way off.

347
00:20:52,502 --> 00:20:54,295
-Now…
-I've got this, Ma.

348
00:20:54,379 --> 00:20:56,172
I just got my talent's fee.

349
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:58,841
Thank goodness!

350
00:20:58,925 --> 00:21:02,762
By the way, your father has
used up all his medicine.

351
00:21:05,723 --> 00:21:08,685
-Two hundred fifty. Here.
-Oh, thank you, big sis!

352
00:21:08,768 --> 00:21:10,019
Mm-hmm.

353
00:21:10,561 --> 00:21:13,022
Just make sure you study well.

354
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:15,984
Be like April. Always top of the class.

355
00:21:16,401 --> 00:21:19,278
-Hey, I'm consistent too.
-Hmm?

356
00:21:19,362 --> 00:21:21,030
-Consistently the class muse. Bam!
-Whoa.

357
00:21:21,114 --> 00:21:23,282
My goodness.

358
00:21:23,366 --> 00:21:24,575
Look at her.

359
00:21:24,659 --> 00:21:27,286
She's destined to be a beauty queen.

360
00:21:27,370 --> 00:21:31,124
And once April graduates,

361
00:21:31,207 --> 00:21:34,043
I'll be living like royalty.

362
00:21:34,127 --> 00:21:39,257
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

363
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:44,512
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

364
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:50,143
♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪

365
00:21:50,685 --> 00:21:55,732
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

366
00:21:58,151 --> 00:21:59,777
Happy birthday, dear.

367
00:22:01,863 --> 00:22:03,823
Come on, blow out the candle.

368
00:22:03,906 --> 00:22:06,451
But wait, you have to make a wish first.

369
00:22:11,831 --> 00:22:14,000
Happy birthday, big sis!

370
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:15,376
Thank you, Papa.

371
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:17,837
I forgot it's your birthday.

372
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:20,673
My goodness. Why didn't you tell me?

373
00:22:20,757 --> 00:22:24,093
Patricia, you should've said something.

374
00:22:24,177 --> 00:22:27,388
I could've made noodles.

375
00:22:27,472 --> 00:22:29,599
I've had so much on my mind

376
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:31,100
that I overlooked it.

377
00:22:31,184 --> 00:22:33,144
-I'm sorry.
-It's all right, Ma.

378
00:22:33,227 --> 00:22:35,605
You know I don't want any celebration.

379
00:22:35,688 --> 00:22:37,023
-Dear…
-Yes?

380
00:22:38,149 --> 00:22:39,942
-What is that?
-Oh…

381
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:42,528
Who hurt you? Tell me who did this!

382
00:22:42,612 --> 00:22:44,197
Hey, hey! Pa, calm down!

383
00:22:45,531 --> 00:22:48,242
We shot some action-heavy stuff,

384
00:22:48,326 --> 00:22:50,328
but don't worry. It's nothing major.

385
00:22:50,411 --> 00:22:53,873
So when do we get to see your scenes?

386
00:22:54,791 --> 00:22:56,793
Forget it. You won't even
see my face there.

387
00:22:56,876 --> 00:22:58,753
I was just the lead star's body double.

388
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:00,630
So you can't even watch your own work?

389
00:23:01,881 --> 00:23:05,218
All I know is that someday…

390
00:23:05,968 --> 00:23:07,595
you'll be the star.

391
00:23:08,763 --> 00:23:10,598
Let's dig in! It looks delicious!

392
00:23:10,681 --> 00:23:13,643
Psst, wait. Let your sister eat first.

393
00:23:14,602 --> 00:23:17,438
Seems like you've got a drink ready, Pa.

394
00:23:17,522 --> 00:23:20,149
Uh, well… It's your birthday.

395
00:23:20,233 --> 00:23:21,442
So, let's celebrate.

396
00:23:21,776 --> 00:23:23,778
-Hmm? You want to celebrate?
-Mm-hmm.

397
00:23:23,861 --> 00:23:25,571
Well, my birthday wish
is for you to quit drinking.

398
00:23:25,655 --> 00:23:27,657
-Come on.
-Nope, just stick to water.

399
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:28,950
-Right, Ma?
-Mm-hmm.

400
00:23:29,033 --> 00:23:30,243
That's right.

401
00:23:39,043 --> 00:23:40,586
Cut the pie later.

402
00:23:44,715 --> 00:23:45,925
It's raw…

403
00:23:49,137 --> 00:23:50,388
Call the chef.

404
00:23:53,141 --> 00:23:55,059
-Walk faster.
-Yes, Ms. D?

405
00:23:57,186 --> 00:23:58,437
This is raw.

406
00:23:58,813 --> 00:24:00,982
It's just a little bit pink…

407
00:24:03,609 --> 00:24:06,404
Of all the things I hate, it's excuses.

408
00:24:07,530 --> 00:24:09,198
This is turkey. Poultry.

409
00:24:09,282 --> 00:24:11,868
And isn't poultry
never served undercooked?

410
00:24:12,201 --> 00:24:13,536
Do you want to give me salmonella?

411
00:24:13,619 --> 00:24:16,789
Do you want me dead? You sit down.

412
00:24:18,583 --> 00:24:20,585
-Ma'am?
-Sit down!

413
00:24:24,839 --> 00:24:26,007
Taste it.

414
00:24:33,556 --> 00:24:34,932
Delicious?

415
00:24:36,267 --> 00:24:37,310
Mmm!

416
00:24:44,859 --> 00:24:47,195
It's mine! I washed the dishes!

417
00:24:47,278 --> 00:24:48,779
I scrubbed the bathroom!

418
00:24:52,033 --> 00:24:53,534
Stop it, you two.

419
00:24:53,993 --> 00:24:58,706
Give it to your sister,
she's exhausted from work.

420
00:24:58,789 --> 00:25:00,958
Go on, have some more.
It's your day. Don't be shy.

421
00:25:01,042 --> 00:25:02,501
It's okay. That's for you.

422
00:25:08,424 --> 00:25:11,469
There, nice and even.

423
00:25:11,886 --> 00:25:13,554
Everyone gets some. Here you go.

424
00:25:13,638 --> 00:25:15,681
You're the best, big sis.

425
00:25:15,765 --> 00:25:18,517
She's practically a saint.

426
00:25:24,857 --> 00:25:26,943
You okay, Pa?
You're out of water. Wait, I'll get some.

427
00:25:29,070 --> 00:25:31,197
Martin Dela Cruz,
come out and face us!

428
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:33,157
-That's right!
-Show your face!

429
00:25:33,241 --> 00:25:35,451
-Get out here!
-Come outside!

430
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:43,042
Captain, what's the matter?

431
00:25:43,125 --> 00:25:45,670
Your father took all of our money!

432
00:25:45,753 --> 00:25:46,837
What?

433
00:25:48,714 --> 00:25:50,591
-Pa.
-He said…

434
00:25:50,675 --> 00:25:54,387
he'd help us get a livelihood package
from the government,

435
00:25:54,470 --> 00:25:55,972
and we just needed
to pay a processing fee!

436
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:58,057
So we gave money to your father!

437
00:25:58,140 --> 00:26:01,060
But then we learned it was all a lie!

438
00:26:01,143 --> 00:26:03,312
-Exactly!
-Liar!

439
00:26:03,396 --> 00:26:05,398
And you're probably
in cahoots with Carlota!

440
00:26:05,481 --> 00:26:07,191
After all, she works at the town hall!

441
00:26:07,275 --> 00:26:09,610
Hey, that's quite an accusation!

442
00:26:09,694 --> 00:26:11,612
Martin is innocent!

443
00:26:11,696 --> 00:26:14,532
Mr. Dimayuga is behind it all!

444
00:26:14,615 --> 00:26:15,783
I don't know a thing!

445
00:26:15,866 --> 00:26:17,827
He has your money!

446
00:26:17,910 --> 00:26:19,870
Dimayuga has been arrested!

447
00:26:19,954 --> 00:26:21,706
He said you still
haven't given him his cut!

448
00:26:21,789 --> 00:26:23,040
Don't play dumb!

449
00:26:23,124 --> 00:26:24,417
-That's right!
-Yes!

450
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:28,254
-Pa…
-Such a liar.

451
00:26:28,337 --> 00:26:30,923
What are they talking about?
What did you do with their money?

452
00:26:31,007 --> 00:26:32,842
Oh, please!
Don't pretend you know nothing!

453
00:26:32,925 --> 00:26:35,094
I-I honestly didn't know!

454
00:26:35,177 --> 00:26:37,680
Well, we know your family's deep in debt!

455
00:26:37,763 --> 00:26:40,016
No wonder, you're all desperate!

456
00:26:40,099 --> 00:26:42,601
You all deserve to be locked up!

457
00:26:42,685 --> 00:26:43,853
-Right?
-Yes!

458
00:26:43,936 --> 00:26:46,063
Come on, you don't need to do this.

459
00:26:46,147 --> 00:26:48,441
He should rot in prison!

460
00:26:48,524 --> 00:26:51,235
-Explain yourself, Martin!
-Hang on…

461
00:26:51,319 --> 00:26:52,945
Wait a minute!

462
00:26:53,029 --> 00:26:55,239
-Sir, please wait!
-That's him, sir!

463
00:26:55,323 --> 00:26:57,783
Martin Dela Cruz,
come with us to the police station.

464
00:26:57,867 --> 00:26:58,868
Wait, wait!

465
00:26:58,951 --> 00:27:00,911
-Please, hang on!
-Wait a second!

466
00:27:00,995 --> 00:27:02,455
Lock him up!

467
00:27:02,538 --> 00:27:03,748
-Mister!
-Hold on!

468
00:27:03,831 --> 00:27:06,709
-Hold on!
-Don't hurt him!

469
00:27:06,792 --> 00:27:07,918
Sir, take him!

470
00:27:10,004 --> 00:27:13,007
Consider that your last meal
in this house.

471
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:15,634
Ma'am?

472
00:27:15,718 --> 00:27:18,179
I don't have to prove myself
right all the time.

473
00:27:18,262 --> 00:27:19,263
You're fired.

474
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:24,143
Hello?

475
00:27:25,436 --> 00:27:28,898
Ms. D… Something went wrong
with the feeding program.

476
00:27:29,482 --> 00:27:30,900
What went wrong?

477
00:27:32,526 --> 00:27:34,570
There was food poisoning
at our feeding program

478
00:27:34,653 --> 00:27:35,696
in Corpuz City.

479
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:37,823
They're pointing to Cala Soda
as the cause.

480
00:27:37,907 --> 00:27:39,533
-What?
-There are already 125 victims

481
00:27:39,617 --> 00:27:41,994
and still counting.
It's severe food poisoning, Ms. D.

482
00:27:42,078 --> 00:27:44,455
Most of the victims
are children and the elderly.

483
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:47,750
Is it confirmed that our soda
is the source of poisoning?

484
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:49,210
Final lab results
are yet to be announced,

485
00:27:49,293 --> 00:27:52,004
but the initial reports suggest
possible soda contamination.

486
00:27:52,088 --> 00:27:54,632
Possible is not an answer.

487
00:27:54,715 --> 00:27:57,009
From which plant was the product sourced?

488
00:27:57,093 --> 00:27:58,344
Uh… Uh…

489
00:27:58,427 --> 00:27:59,929
I will confirm that right now, Ms. D.

490
00:28:00,012 --> 00:28:02,181
Shouldn't you have already
known that before I asked?

491
00:28:02,264 --> 00:28:03,974
Give me an answer!

492
00:28:04,058 --> 00:28:06,102
We've been in contact
with the hospital management

493
00:28:06,185 --> 00:28:07,686
and the families of the victims.

494
00:28:07,770 --> 00:28:09,605
We'll be responsible
for their hospital bills.

495
00:28:09,688 --> 00:28:12,608
Call the legal department. Have them
prepare the compensation packages.

496
00:28:12,691 --> 00:28:14,026
Noted, Ms. D.

497
00:28:14,110 --> 00:28:17,238
Ms. D?
Burger City International is on the phone.

498
00:28:19,365 --> 00:28:20,574
This is Diana Aragon.

499
00:28:21,575 --> 00:28:23,536
Diana,
I'm gonna cut straight to the point.

500
00:28:23,619 --> 00:28:24,745
We're very disappointed.

501
00:28:24,829 --> 00:28:28,833
The initial launch… was unfortunate.
But manageable.

502
00:28:28,916 --> 00:28:30,876
This situation is under control.

503
00:28:30,960 --> 00:28:32,169
Investigation is underway.

504
00:28:32,253 --> 00:28:34,713
Children being poisoned
is not a "situation."

505
00:28:34,797 --> 00:28:36,590
Burger City International
cannot be affiliated

506
00:28:36,674 --> 00:28:37,758
with that kind of controversy.

507
00:28:37,842 --> 00:28:38,884
No, no, no.

508
00:28:38,968 --> 00:28:40,928
Give me 24 hours. We can fix this.

509
00:28:41,011 --> 00:28:42,304
We're fix-- We're on this.

510
00:28:42,388 --> 00:28:44,348
The board has already made its decision.

511
00:28:44,432 --> 00:28:46,725
We're terminating our partnership,
effective immediately.

512
00:28:46,809 --> 00:28:47,977
I'm sorry, Diana.

513
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:49,937
No, no, no, but--

514
00:28:53,107 --> 00:28:55,025
-Call them again.
-Yes, ma'am.

515
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:56,444
Georgia is calling them right now.

516
00:28:58,571 --> 00:28:59,905
Auntie.

517
00:29:00,781 --> 00:29:02,700
Auntie, they're not answering anymore.

518
00:29:04,660 --> 00:29:06,287
No response either, Ms. D.

519
00:29:20,426 --> 00:29:23,637
Can anyone tell me what caused this?

520
00:29:24,263 --> 00:29:27,141
Does anybody here know
what caused this thing?

521
00:29:27,224 --> 00:29:28,642
This whole thing? No one?

522
00:29:28,726 --> 00:29:29,935
Nothing?

523
00:29:30,352 --> 00:29:33,689
Do you even know
what's at stake in this deal?

524
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:35,107
Now I'm losing it

525
00:29:35,191 --> 00:29:37,568
because you can't give me an answer!

526
00:29:37,902 --> 00:29:40,488
Did I hire freaking imbeciles?

527
00:29:40,571 --> 00:29:42,656
How did this happen?

528
00:29:42,740 --> 00:29:46,660
I cannot--
I will not lose this partnership deal!

529
00:29:46,744 --> 00:29:48,537
I need to get to the bottom of this!

530
00:29:48,621 --> 00:29:50,664
Right now! I need answers!

531
00:29:50,748 --> 00:29:52,416
Give me answers!

532
00:29:58,130 --> 00:29:59,340
-Ms. D…
-Ms. D?

533
00:29:59,423 --> 00:30:00,466
-Ms. D!
-Diana! Diana!

534
00:30:00,549 --> 00:30:01,759
-Ms. D!
-Auntie!

535
00:30:01,842 --> 00:30:03,427
-Call an ambulance!
-Get an ambulance!

536
00:30:03,511 --> 00:30:05,888
Hurry! Ms. D? Ms. D?

537
00:30:05,971 --> 00:30:07,515
Diana…

538
00:30:09,016 --> 00:30:10,226
Patient still has no pulse.

539
00:30:10,309 --> 00:30:12,603
-Showing signs of V-tach.
-Continue CPR.

540
00:30:13,145 --> 00:30:14,146
-Charge the defibrillator…
-No pulse.

541
00:30:14,230 --> 00:30:15,523
to 200 joules, biphasic.

542
00:30:16,524 --> 00:30:18,234
-Three. Everybody clear?
-Clear!

543
00:30:26,075 --> 00:30:27,117
ELECTRICITY ₱1,650
WATER ₱700

544
00:30:28,953 --> 00:30:29,954
RENT ₱3,000

545
00:30:32,122 --> 00:30:33,165
SAVINGS FOR TUITION ₱2,000

546
00:30:49,056 --> 00:30:51,100
Don't tell me
you'll spend that too.

547
00:30:52,518 --> 00:30:54,520
You've been saving that for months.

548
00:30:54,603 --> 00:30:56,021
For rent.

549
00:30:56,397 --> 00:30:58,732
And weren't you setting aside
money for tuition

550
00:30:58,816 --> 00:31:01,151
because you want to study again?

551
00:31:01,902 --> 00:31:03,279
I'll just save up again.

552
00:31:04,446 --> 00:31:07,157
What matters is that
we post bail for Papa.

553
00:31:07,241 --> 00:31:09,535
But big sis… Will that be enough?

554
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:11,245
I'm not really sure.

555
00:31:18,836 --> 00:31:21,589
-I'll pawn this too.
-And then what?

556
00:31:21,672 --> 00:31:24,550
Once it's pawned, will that cover it?

557
00:31:26,594 --> 00:31:29,638
Isn't there a popular lending app?

558
00:31:29,722 --> 00:31:30,973
Help me download it.

559
00:31:31,056 --> 00:31:32,641
But they've got a high interest rate.

560
00:31:32,725 --> 00:31:34,602
We can worry about that later.

561
00:31:35,019 --> 00:31:38,689
I hate this life!
Why did we have to be born poor?

562
00:31:39,106 --> 00:31:42,359
I wish we were nepo babies,
swimming in money.

563
00:31:42,443 --> 00:31:47,573
Or the missing heirs
with a grandfather searching for us

564
00:31:48,324 --> 00:31:50,117
to give us everything! That kind of life!

565
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:52,494
That only happens in the movies, Jena.

566
00:31:52,578 --> 00:31:54,997
Where someone has to die
before the heiress inherits.

567
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:57,541
Where did I even see that?
On Facegram, right?

568
00:31:57,625 --> 00:31:59,501
-Was it there?
-Let me help.

569
00:31:59,585 --> 00:32:01,629
Let's check. Wait.

570
00:32:01,712 --> 00:32:02,921
Hang on, what's this?

571
00:32:03,005 --> 00:32:04,340
We are currently at Central Crest Hospital

572
00:32:04,423 --> 00:32:08,052
and Medical Center, where the CEO
of La Familia Bottling Company

573
00:32:08,135 --> 00:32:10,929
is reportedly confined.

574
00:32:11,013 --> 00:32:12,306
Based on initial reports,

575
00:32:12,389 --> 00:32:16,268
Diana Aragon,
known as the "Chairmom" of La Familia,

576
00:32:16,352 --> 00:32:20,147
suffered a heart attack
after the issue of food poisoning

577
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:22,191
in one of their feeding programs erupted.

578
00:32:22,274 --> 00:32:26,236
Cala Soda is being pointed to
as the cause of the poisoning.

579
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:28,697
We are still waiting for a statement

580
00:32:28,781 --> 00:32:31,033
from her brother, Teodoro Aragon.

581
00:32:31,492 --> 00:32:34,912
Aside from him, Ms. Aragon
has no other immediate family.

582
00:32:34,995 --> 00:32:37,247
But according to the information
we gathered,

583
00:32:37,623 --> 00:32:40,376
Ms. Aragon has a daughter.

584
00:32:40,459 --> 00:32:43,128
Wow. A missing daughter?

585
00:32:43,879 --> 00:32:46,632
Lucky her! She's an instant heiress!

586
00:32:46,715 --> 00:32:48,801
In the midst
of the uncertain situation,

587
00:32:48,884 --> 00:32:50,302
the question on everyone's minds is:

588
00:32:50,803 --> 00:32:55,307
where is the sole heiress of La Familia?

589
00:33:00,437 --> 00:33:02,856
Mama!

590
00:33:02,940 --> 00:33:04,233
Ma'am…

591
00:33:04,316 --> 00:33:06,276
Excuse me. Who are you?

592
00:33:06,360 --> 00:33:08,904
Sir, I'm the real daughter
of Diana Aragon!

593
00:33:08,987 --> 00:33:10,572
Where is my mother?

594
00:33:10,656 --> 00:33:12,324
-Where--
-No, that's not true!

595
00:33:12,408 --> 00:33:15,119
I'm the real daughter of Diana Aragon!

596
00:33:15,202 --> 00:33:17,287
-Excuse--
-Hang on! Don't believe them!

597
00:33:17,371 --> 00:33:19,373
I'm her real daughter!
Do they look rich at all?

598
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:22,376
Wait a minute--

599
00:33:37,725 --> 00:33:39,601
-Argh! Nurse, my stomach hurts!
-What's wrong, ma'am?

600
00:33:41,145 --> 00:33:43,147
Let me wheel you in.

601
00:33:48,986 --> 00:33:52,364
Excuse me. Excuse me.

602
00:33:52,448 --> 00:33:53,741
Excuse me!

603
00:33:53,824 --> 00:33:56,285
Excuse me! Everyone, listen up!

604
00:33:56,368 --> 00:33:59,455
Have some respect for Ms. D.

605
00:33:59,538 --> 00:34:03,459
Please.
You all need to go right now, okay?

606
00:34:03,542 --> 00:34:04,585
-Guards, please.
-Yes, sir.

607
00:34:04,668 --> 00:34:07,796
Hey, Daryl!
Dr. Reyes has been looking for you.

608
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:09,173
I have a patient.

609
00:34:09,256 --> 00:34:11,341
Uh, no, you can leave me now.

610
00:34:11,425 --> 00:34:13,719
-Are you sure you'll be okay?
-Yes. Thank you.

611
00:34:13,802 --> 00:34:15,679
-All right, then.
-Brace yourself.

612
00:34:15,763 --> 00:34:17,139
-Just leave, ma'am.
-This way, please.

613
00:34:17,222 --> 00:34:19,183
Guards, please secure the perimeter.

614
00:34:19,266 --> 00:34:20,476
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

615
00:34:29,735 --> 00:34:30,986
Excuse me.

616
00:34:32,863 --> 00:34:34,114
Excuse me!

617
00:34:39,286 --> 00:34:41,538
Unbelievable!

618
00:34:41,622 --> 00:34:43,665
Didn't we already tell you press people?

619
00:34:43,749 --> 00:34:46,001
-No coverage for now.
-Just one question, sir.

620
00:34:46,084 --> 00:34:48,253
We're not ready to make
a statement at this time.

621
00:34:48,712 --> 00:34:49,671
Okay?

622
00:34:49,755 --> 00:34:51,965
Please, get out of here.

623
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:02,893
Jena.

624
00:35:03,477 --> 00:35:04,186
Pa!

625
00:35:04,812 --> 00:35:06,855
Pa, you're back!

626
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:10,692
-Pa!
-Oh, sweetie.

627
00:35:10,776 --> 00:35:12,361
How was it? Are you okay?

628
00:35:12,444 --> 00:35:14,404
Wasn't the bed uncomfortable?

629
00:35:14,488 --> 00:35:15,864
Wasn't it hot there, Pa?

630
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:18,367
It was a little hot, but I'm fine.

631
00:35:18,784 --> 00:35:21,912
-I'm just worried about your feet…
-Pa…

632
00:35:21,995 --> 00:35:25,707
Oh, they missed you so much.

633
00:35:27,543 --> 00:35:30,170
-I'll make you a cup of coffee.
-Thanks.

634
00:35:31,588 --> 00:35:33,215
How'd your night go?

635
00:35:34,216 --> 00:35:36,677
We're out of coffee.
Did you ask your sister to buy some?

636
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,136
Oh, my!

637
00:35:38,220 --> 00:35:40,556
Ma, I reminded her.

638
00:35:41,598 --> 00:35:44,768
But she might've forgotten
while fixing Papa's mess.

639
00:35:46,478 --> 00:35:50,232
Look, Pa… I'm glad she found a way
to cover your bail.

640
00:35:50,315 --> 00:35:51,525
Hold on.

641
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:53,819
Where did she get the money?

642
00:35:55,153 --> 00:35:58,490
She used her savings, and borrowed money.

643
00:35:59,199 --> 00:36:01,827
She even pawned her necklace.

644
00:36:03,996 --> 00:36:05,956
I'll just pay her back.

645
00:36:06,290 --> 00:36:08,333
Where's your sister, anyway?

646
00:36:10,586 --> 00:36:12,629
I have no idea, Ma.

647
00:36:48,707 --> 00:36:51,251
She said she'd be here.

648
00:36:51,335 --> 00:36:53,503
I was the only one without a mom.

649
00:36:56,632 --> 00:37:00,344
Mama probably has important work
at the office, dear.

650
00:37:01,136 --> 00:37:03,931
More important than me?

651
00:37:04,014 --> 00:37:06,183
At least Papa is here.

652
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:08,602
Come on, Papa.

653
00:37:08,685 --> 00:37:12,397
It's Mother's Day. You're not a mother.

654
00:37:12,481 --> 00:37:14,274
Hey, I have an idea.

655
00:37:15,108 --> 00:37:16,610
Let's go get ice cream.

656
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:20,614
Even though
Mama says sweets are bad for me?

657
00:37:20,697 --> 00:37:25,577
We'll keep it our little secret.
Okay?

658
00:37:43,387 --> 00:37:44,805
You need this.

659
00:37:44,888 --> 00:37:47,099
Thank you.

660
00:37:47,182 --> 00:37:49,142
Is it obvious my head hurts?

661
00:37:49,226 --> 00:37:53,647
I've memorized
every wrinkle on your forehead.

662
00:37:54,189 --> 00:37:56,525
You don't need to keep doing this.

663
00:37:56,608 --> 00:37:58,402
You're already the company's bookkeeper.

664
00:37:58,485 --> 00:38:02,072
Does that mean I should stop
being friends with you?

665
00:38:02,155 --> 00:38:03,240
Of course not.

666
00:38:05,117 --> 00:38:07,452
I wonder how I would manage without you.

667
00:38:10,580 --> 00:38:12,958
Oh, could you take this off?

668
00:38:13,041 --> 00:38:15,210
-Help me, please.
-Why?

669
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:17,546
Doesn't it go better with your dress?

670
00:38:19,923 --> 00:38:23,802
Are you sure?
What, is this a loan or a gift?

671
00:38:23,885 --> 00:38:25,679
It's a gift, obviously.
Never a loan.

672
00:38:33,270 --> 00:38:35,772
Excuse me. Patricia.

673
00:38:35,856 --> 00:38:37,274
What are you doing?

674
00:38:37,357 --> 00:38:39,401
I want to blow out the candle now.

675
00:38:39,484 --> 00:38:42,863
My gosh! Will you stop it? Please!

676
00:38:44,698 --> 00:38:48,577
You never use just your hands
when you eat, okay?

677
00:38:48,660 --> 00:38:50,120
You have to keep yourself neat

678
00:38:50,203 --> 00:38:52,205
and clean and presentable.

679
00:38:52,289 --> 00:38:54,082
Look at Enzo and Georgia over there.

680
00:38:54,166 --> 00:38:55,375
They're well-behaved.

681
00:38:55,459 --> 00:38:57,961
They actually listen
to what their parents say.

682
00:38:58,420 --> 00:39:02,174
I just don't understand why
you're so stubborn, dear.

683
00:39:02,257 --> 00:39:04,301
What's the use of being an Aragon

684
00:39:04,384 --> 00:39:06,470
if Papa can't trust me
to lead the company?

685
00:39:07,137 --> 00:39:08,180
-Am I right?
-Absolutely.

686
00:39:08,263 --> 00:39:10,474
But you know what? One day…

687
00:39:10,557 --> 00:39:12,017
I want to move away from the shadows

688
00:39:12,100 --> 00:39:13,477
and build my own company.

689
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:15,937
-That's the spirit.
-I know, right?

690
00:39:16,021 --> 00:39:18,398
Where's the dress I bought for you?

691
00:39:18,482 --> 00:39:20,067
Why are you wearing this?

692
00:39:20,817 --> 00:39:22,235
It was itchy.

693
00:39:22,569 --> 00:39:24,237
Plus, it's my birthday.

694
00:39:24,321 --> 00:39:25,781
Exactly, dear. It's your birthday.

695
00:39:25,864 --> 00:39:28,200
You should've worn it.
It's a pretty dress.

696
00:39:28,283 --> 00:39:29,785
You're very pretty. What a waste!

697
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:32,829
And now look at you.
You stained your outfit.

698
00:39:32,913 --> 00:39:34,956
That's fine.

699
00:39:35,040 --> 00:39:37,167
Martin, look at what she did to the cake.

700
00:39:37,626 --> 00:39:40,462
She poked it.
She poked it and had a taste.

701
00:39:40,545 --> 00:39:42,172
She stained her outfit.
She destroyed the cake.

702
00:39:42,255 --> 00:39:43,465
Now it's all ruined.

703
00:39:43,548 --> 00:39:45,342
Oh, relax.

704
00:39:45,425 --> 00:39:47,719
This is why your daughter never learns.

705
00:39:47,803 --> 00:39:49,721
Patricia is just a kid.

706
00:39:49,805 --> 00:39:51,932
Let her have fun.

707
00:39:52,015 --> 00:39:53,225
It's her birthday today.

708
00:39:53,308 --> 00:39:56,103
Sure, but when will she learn?
When she's all grown up?

709
00:39:56,186 --> 00:40:01,191
-Come on now.
-Hey… My wife's way too serious.

710
00:40:01,274 --> 00:40:03,360
-Oh, please.
-Come on.

711
00:40:03,443 --> 00:40:05,529
I'll look after Patricia.

712
00:40:05,612 --> 00:40:07,322
I'll take care of her.

713
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:08,615
Let me.

714
00:40:09,366 --> 00:40:13,078
Martin, stay with Diana.
She's been stressed out.

715
00:40:13,161 --> 00:40:15,455
Fine, team up against me again.

716
00:40:15,539 --> 00:40:16,915
Oh, you two.

717
00:40:16,998 --> 00:40:18,041
-Martin!
-Hmm?

718
00:40:18,125 --> 00:40:19,209
What are you doing?

719
00:40:19,292 --> 00:40:22,838
Papa doesn't want you smoking! Put it out!

720
00:40:22,921 --> 00:40:25,090
Fine, fine. I won't smoke.

721
00:40:25,173 --> 00:40:27,134
How much did you drink?

722
00:40:27,634 --> 00:40:29,553
Fix yourself, hmm?

723
00:40:30,679 --> 00:40:33,640
-Oh, I need to…
-Hey.

724
00:40:34,766 --> 00:40:36,476
-What?
-You know the drill.

725
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:38,103
-Oh, my gosh, Martin.
-Let's dance.

726
00:40:38,186 --> 00:40:40,105
-It's embarrassing.
-Come here.

727
00:40:40,188 --> 00:40:42,566
-You've too much-- See?
-Hold on.

728
00:40:42,649 --> 00:40:43,900
-Hold on.
-Argh.

729
00:40:44,860 --> 00:40:46,778
See? How much did you drink?

730
00:40:46,862 --> 00:40:48,530
-Let's enjoy!
-How much did you drink?

731
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:50,490
-Come on, turn. Turn.
- Stop it!

732
00:40:53,577 --> 00:40:55,328
-Yes! Yes!
-I think you're drunk.

733
00:41:08,008 --> 00:41:09,009
Sorry, sir.

734
00:41:10,385 --> 00:41:12,095
-Excuse me.
-Oh, sure, sure.

735
00:41:12,179 --> 00:41:13,972
I'm sorry. Don't mind it.

736
00:41:14,639 --> 00:41:16,308
Nothing to worry about.
It's just wine glass.

737
00:41:16,391 --> 00:41:17,559
We have a lot of it.

738
00:41:17,642 --> 00:41:19,561
And we have more drinks,

739
00:41:19,644 --> 00:41:21,271
so let's keep the party going.

740
00:41:22,189 --> 00:41:25,692
I think you got this all wrong.

741
00:41:26,359 --> 00:41:27,986
This isn't a family day event.

742
00:41:29,863 --> 00:41:33,074
This event was created for business.

743
00:41:33,909 --> 00:41:37,495
Maybe you forgot that it's also
your granddaughter's birthday today.

744
00:41:37,579 --> 00:41:41,458
Don't you have any other necklace
that isn't tacky?

745
00:41:42,167 --> 00:41:43,501
Come on, dear.

746
00:41:44,002 --> 00:41:45,128
Diana, let's go.

747
00:41:46,504 --> 00:41:47,714
Diana.

748
00:41:48,423 --> 00:41:50,634
Attorney Ignacio is here

749
00:41:50,717 --> 00:41:52,802
and we need to talk to him.

750
00:41:52,886 --> 00:41:54,095
This is important.

751
00:41:55,555 --> 00:41:57,974
Follow me. Now.

752
00:42:09,945 --> 00:42:12,197
The company started

753
00:42:13,114 --> 00:42:14,366
as an sugar mill.

754
00:42:15,575 --> 00:42:19,496
Until we ventured into drinks.

755
00:42:20,538 --> 00:42:23,792
Since then, we have been loved
by every Filipino

756
00:42:23,875 --> 00:42:26,670
across many generations.

757
00:42:27,254 --> 00:42:31,967
Tonight is not just about looking back.

758
00:42:33,885 --> 00:42:36,554
Tonight is also about looking forward.

759
00:42:36,638 --> 00:42:40,850
Because a family business

760
00:42:41,309 --> 00:42:44,938
isn't just passed down

761
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:46,856
to the next generation.

762
00:42:48,024 --> 00:42:50,318
It should be protected

763
00:42:51,319 --> 00:42:53,113
and preserved.

764
00:42:53,196 --> 00:42:55,115
Long live La Familia!

765
00:42:57,367 --> 00:42:58,535
Hey, Martin.

766
00:43:00,912 --> 00:43:02,914
Martin, stop it. It's embarrassing.

767
00:43:02,998 --> 00:43:04,749
Get it together.

768
00:43:04,833 --> 00:43:06,167
And now,

769
00:43:07,085 --> 00:43:08,878
for the success

770
00:43:08,962 --> 00:43:11,673
of our newest product.

771
00:43:12,465 --> 00:43:14,384
The Cala Soda.

772
00:43:14,467 --> 00:43:18,096
A product years in development.

773
00:43:18,930 --> 00:43:21,016
And only reminds us

774
00:43:21,099 --> 00:43:23,810
that legacy can't be inherited.

775
00:43:24,185 --> 00:43:27,814
It is something one must work hard for.

776
00:43:31,026 --> 00:43:32,193
Martin!

777
00:43:32,277 --> 00:43:33,903
-Papa!
-Martin, please.

778
00:43:33,987 --> 00:43:35,280
I'm so sorry.

779
00:43:35,947 --> 00:43:37,032
-I'm okay.
-M-Martin…

780
00:43:37,115 --> 00:43:38,366
Cheers, Lucio!

781
00:43:38,450 --> 00:43:40,410
To other people's hard work

782
00:43:40,493 --> 00:43:43,788
that's been taken advantage of
by a greedy family!

783
00:43:44,372 --> 00:43:47,876
The shameless family, the Aragons!

784
00:43:47,959 --> 00:43:49,836
See this?

785
00:43:49,919 --> 00:43:51,171
Do you see this?

786
00:43:51,254 --> 00:43:53,757
This Cala Soda? It's mine!

787
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,258
It came from me!

788
00:43:55,342 --> 00:43:57,927
I made the recipe!

789
00:43:58,011 --> 00:44:01,097
But after all the hard work I put into it,

790
00:44:02,140 --> 00:44:05,268
he promoted his daughter instead!

791
00:44:05,643 --> 00:44:07,312
And when I complained,

792
00:44:07,395 --> 00:44:11,358
they had the guts to fire me!

793
00:44:11,733 --> 00:44:13,610
Guards, get this woman out!

794
00:44:13,693 --> 00:44:15,111
I'm telling the truth!

795
00:44:15,195 --> 00:44:16,196
-You are thieves!
-Hurry up!

796
00:44:16,279 --> 00:44:18,615
-It's okay, it's okay.
-You're all thieves!

797
00:44:18,698 --> 00:44:20,825
Liars!

798
00:44:47,394 --> 00:44:51,689
Happy birthday to me

799
00:44:52,482 --> 00:44:56,820
♪ Happy birthday to me ♪

800
00:44:57,445 --> 00:44:59,614
Happy birthday, Patricia!

801
00:45:21,845 --> 00:45:23,680
Damn it. You're not being careful.

802
00:45:23,763 --> 00:45:25,390
Hurry up and fix it.

803
00:45:26,015 --> 00:45:27,600
Put in the recycle bin.

804
00:45:27,684 --> 00:45:29,978
Hurry and get it all off so I can go.

805
00:45:34,107 --> 00:45:35,692
Oh, my cake!

806
00:45:42,949 --> 00:45:43,950
Ah!

807
00:45:58,423 --> 00:46:00,842
Help!

808
00:46:09,726 --> 00:46:12,520
-Mama!
-Dear!

809
00:46:12,604 --> 00:46:13,980
Let's get out of here, dear!

810
00:46:19,819 --> 00:46:21,446
-Carry her there!
-Let's go!

811
00:46:21,946 --> 00:46:26,451
Mommy! Mommy! Mommy!

812
00:46:26,534 --> 00:46:29,329
-Oh, my god.
-Mommy! Mommy!

813
00:46:29,412 --> 00:46:31,873
Diana! Diana!

814
00:46:31,956 --> 00:46:33,333
-Diana, are you okay?
-Carlota!

815
00:46:33,416 --> 00:46:36,294
Where's Papa?
Does he know what's going on here?

816
00:46:37,003 --> 00:46:39,797
I haven't seen him since the party.

817
00:46:39,881 --> 00:46:41,966
-But I'll ask around.
-Please do!

818
00:46:42,050 --> 00:46:44,093
Find out if he already knows,
then tell me.

819
00:46:44,177 --> 00:46:45,470
Okay, okay.

820
00:46:45,553 --> 00:46:46,804
You all right?

821
00:46:46,888 --> 00:46:48,473
Just stay here, okay?

822
00:46:48,556 --> 00:46:50,433
I'll go inside to help.

823
00:46:50,517 --> 00:46:51,976
-Okay.
-Look after Patricia.

824
00:46:52,060 --> 00:46:53,353
Yes, I got her.

825
00:46:56,523 --> 00:46:57,690
What's this?

826
00:47:00,985 --> 00:47:02,779
Why do you have this?

827
00:47:03,905 --> 00:47:06,574
-Huh?
-It's for the candle on my cake.

828
00:47:08,785 --> 00:47:10,537
Where did you light the candle?

829
00:47:10,620 --> 00:47:12,205
Inside the factory?

830
00:47:12,997 --> 00:47:14,749
Did you light it inside the factory?

831
00:47:16,292 --> 00:47:18,461
Patricia, tell me! What did you do?

832
00:47:18,878 --> 00:47:21,339
Mama, I didn't do it!

833
00:47:32,642 --> 00:47:34,227
It hurts!

834
00:47:34,310 --> 00:47:35,562
Oh, god.

835
00:47:36,479 --> 00:47:38,189
Oh, good god!

836
00:47:39,566 --> 00:47:40,858
Oh, my god.

837
00:47:41,442 --> 00:47:42,694
Oh, my god!

838
00:47:44,112 --> 00:47:46,531
Faster, please!

839
00:47:46,614 --> 00:47:47,740
Hurry! Help him!

840
00:47:50,118 --> 00:47:52,537
-Papa! P-Papa!
-Diana.

841
00:47:52,620 --> 00:47:54,414
Let the rescuers do their jobs.

842
00:47:54,497 --> 00:47:55,915
Let me go! Papa!

843
00:47:56,457 --> 00:48:00,086
Papa!

844
00:48:00,169 --> 00:48:01,671
Diana.

845
00:48:01,754 --> 00:48:03,298
Papa!

846
00:48:03,381 --> 00:48:05,800
Papa!

847
00:48:05,883 --> 00:48:10,555
-Papa!
-Mama!

848
00:48:11,264 --> 00:48:13,433
Let me go! Papa!

849
00:48:14,142 --> 00:48:16,436
-Papa!
-Let them treat him!

850
00:48:31,242 --> 00:48:32,660
I'll get some rest.

851
00:48:41,377 --> 00:48:43,087
Mama…

852
00:48:51,679 --> 00:48:52,597
Hello.

853
00:48:53,556 --> 00:48:56,059
Okay, I'll be there in 30 minutes.

854
00:49:09,113 --> 00:49:11,783
Argh! Do it! Argh!

855
00:49:12,408 --> 00:49:13,534
Argh!

856
00:49:13,618 --> 00:49:15,578
You'll pay for your crimes!

857
00:49:15,662 --> 00:49:17,330
You can't get away from the law!

858
00:49:18,122 --> 00:49:19,874
So this is why you keep failing.

859
00:49:19,957 --> 00:49:21,751
All you do is watch TV.

860
00:49:21,834 --> 00:49:26,214
I thought you were struggling,
that's why I hired a tutor for you.

861
00:49:26,297 --> 00:49:31,260
You answered letter D
for all of the items in your exam.

862
00:49:32,178 --> 00:49:33,513
What really is the problem?

863
00:49:33,596 --> 00:49:35,807
Are you being bullied in school? Tell me.

864
00:49:35,890 --> 00:49:37,433
Is there something wrong
with your teacher?

865
00:49:37,517 --> 00:49:38,810
Do they scold you?

866
00:49:38,893 --> 00:49:41,312
Or do you just refuse to learn?

867
00:49:41,396 --> 00:49:43,940
-Answer me.
-None of the above.

868
00:49:44,023 --> 00:49:46,859
Patricia, I've got a lot
going on right now.

869
00:49:46,943 --> 00:49:49,153
Don't make it any worse, dear!

870
00:49:49,862 --> 00:49:51,781
Did you hear that? "None of the above?"

871
00:49:52,824 --> 00:49:54,450
You have a family
to take care of!

872
00:49:54,534 --> 00:49:57,912
All you do is work
for that freaking company!

873
00:49:57,995 --> 00:49:59,664
"Freaking company?"

874
00:49:59,747 --> 00:50:03,793
The company that supports you-- Us?

875
00:50:03,876 --> 00:50:06,462
I'm not the only one benefiting from it!
All of us do!

876
00:50:06,546 --> 00:50:09,298
Fine, you're better than me!
You are the boss.

877
00:50:09,382 --> 00:50:13,177
But I'm not just your employee,
Diana, I'm your husband!

878
00:50:13,553 --> 00:50:17,140
Even after what you did to me,
you're still my husband.

879
00:50:17,473 --> 00:50:20,893
Have you forgotten, Martin,
how I defended you to Papa?

880
00:50:20,977 --> 00:50:23,688
And how hard I fought for this family?

881
00:50:23,771 --> 00:50:26,190
We wouldn't have any problems

882
00:50:26,274 --> 00:50:28,818
if you weren't a suck-up to your dad!

883
00:50:28,901 --> 00:50:30,653
You should've been
a good wife to me,

884
00:50:30,737 --> 00:50:32,488
and a present mother to your child!

885
00:50:32,572 --> 00:50:36,033
You have a lot more shortcomings
than I do!

886
00:50:36,117 --> 00:50:38,202
Papa was right.

887
00:50:38,286 --> 00:50:40,371
I made a mistake marrying you.

888
00:50:41,539 --> 00:50:44,959
You know what, Martin?
We've been through this over and over.

889
00:50:45,042 --> 00:50:47,628
You've always blamed the company,

890
00:50:47,712 --> 00:50:49,547
and you direct your anger to the company.

891
00:50:49,630 --> 00:50:51,758
I'm tired of fighting about this.

892
00:50:52,884 --> 00:50:54,177
Let's separate.

893
00:50:55,762 --> 00:50:58,181
All right! All right, let's separate!

894
00:50:58,806 --> 00:51:00,683
I'm getting tired of being your husband!

895
00:51:01,100 --> 00:51:02,351
Do you really think

896
00:51:02,435 --> 00:51:04,353
you're the only one suffering
in this relationship?

897
00:51:04,437 --> 00:51:05,730
Well…

898
00:51:06,397 --> 00:51:07,607
then leave.

899
00:51:08,232 --> 00:51:09,484
Leave!

900
00:51:11,736 --> 00:51:12,737
Mama!

901
00:51:12,820 --> 00:51:15,364
Don't ask Papa to leave!

902
00:51:15,448 --> 00:51:18,075
P-Patricia, were you there the whole time?

903
00:51:18,159 --> 00:51:19,827
Dear…

904
00:51:21,078 --> 00:51:23,581
Why are you asking Papa to leave?

905
00:51:24,207 --> 00:51:25,500
Your mama doesn't want me anymore

906
00:51:25,958 --> 00:51:27,543
-because I'm poor.
-Martin!

907
00:51:27,627 --> 00:51:29,712
Am I the only one at fault here?

908
00:51:29,796 --> 00:51:31,756
Now you're throwing me out, and you think

909
00:51:32,089 --> 00:51:35,009
it's a mistake getting married
just because you got pregnant.

910
00:51:35,092 --> 00:51:38,763
You think having Patricia
is a mistake too, is that it?

911
00:51:38,846 --> 00:51:40,973
Martin, don't you dare!

912
00:51:41,057 --> 00:51:43,226
Patricia, dear, please stay outside.

913
00:51:43,309 --> 00:51:45,478
Papa and I need to talk, okay?

914
00:51:45,561 --> 00:51:47,563
You're always mad at Papa!

915
00:51:47,647 --> 00:51:50,191
-You don't love us!
-What?

916
00:51:50,274 --> 00:51:53,861
Please don't go, Papa! I'll come with you!

917
00:51:54,278 --> 00:51:55,988
-Don't leave me with her!
-P-Patricia!

918
00:51:56,072 --> 00:51:57,657
Patricia…

919
00:51:57,740 --> 00:52:00,576
do you really think I'll let that happen?

920
00:52:01,118 --> 00:52:02,286
I'm your mama.

921
00:52:02,370 --> 00:52:06,457
If I stay here, will I be with you?

922
00:52:06,958 --> 00:52:09,252
You're always away!

923
00:52:11,045 --> 00:52:12,672
You don't understand.

924
00:52:13,673 --> 00:52:16,509
You don't understand!

925
00:52:17,343 --> 00:52:20,763
You're blaming me
for what happened to Grandpa!

926
00:52:20,847 --> 00:52:22,348
What did you say?

927
00:52:22,723 --> 00:52:23,724
It's true!

928
00:52:23,808 --> 00:52:27,144
Ever since Grandpa died,
you've always been mad at me!

929
00:52:27,228 --> 00:52:28,521
You don't love me anymore!

930
00:52:28,604 --> 00:52:31,607
You wish I were dead instead of him!

931
00:52:31,691 --> 00:52:33,693
Patricia, don't say that!

932
00:52:38,906 --> 00:52:42,618
Martin, don't. Martin, no. No, Martin!

933
00:52:43,327 --> 00:52:45,204
Martin, give me my daughter!

934
00:52:45,288 --> 00:52:46,455
Martin!

935
00:53:05,182 --> 00:53:08,644
Because your child
is over seven years old,

936
00:53:08,728 --> 00:53:11,063
we need to listen to what she has to say

937
00:53:11,147 --> 00:53:13,482
and give value

938
00:53:13,566 --> 00:53:17,069
to her choice or preference.

939
00:53:20,114 --> 00:53:21,282
Patricia,

940
00:53:22,742 --> 00:53:26,704
do you want to be
with your mama or your papa?

941
00:53:45,640 --> 00:53:47,183
I want to be with Papa.

942
00:54:56,627 --> 00:55:00,256
Nanny Cora, is Diana around?
I need to talk to her.

943
00:55:00,631 --> 00:55:02,925
Carlota, I'm so sorry. She's not here.

944
00:55:03,718 --> 00:55:05,511
Don't lie! I know she's here--

945
00:55:06,178 --> 00:55:08,347
She's right there! Diana!

946
00:55:08,889 --> 00:55:10,307
Diana!

947
00:55:11,267 --> 00:55:12,518
Diana!

948
00:55:12,601 --> 00:55:15,229
Diana, Martin got into an accident!

949
00:55:15,938 --> 00:55:17,857
We need your help!

950
00:55:18,482 --> 00:55:19,775
Ma'am, I'm sorry,
I have to ask you to leave.

951
00:55:19,859 --> 00:55:21,402
Diana!

952
00:55:21,736 --> 00:55:24,655
Diana, please! Help Martin!

953
00:55:24,739 --> 00:55:26,949
-Ma'am, I'm sorry.
-Carlota, just leave.

954
00:55:27,033 --> 00:55:29,869
Ma, let's just go!
Let's just go! They don't want us here!

955
00:55:29,952 --> 00:55:31,162
-They don't want us here!
-Please leave.

956
00:55:31,245 --> 00:55:32,830
-Diana!
-Let's go, Ma!

957
00:55:32,913 --> 00:55:34,415
-Please, Carlota!
-Let's go!

958
00:55:34,498 --> 00:55:36,584
Diana, I'm begging you!

959
00:55:36,667 --> 00:55:40,337
Ma, let's go! I'll find a way!
I got this! Let's go!

960
00:55:49,305 --> 00:55:50,806
Code blue! Code blue!

961
00:55:53,851 --> 00:55:55,144
Ms. D?

962
00:56:02,068 --> 00:56:03,944
Am I not supposed to be here?

963
00:56:04,028 --> 00:56:05,446
I just don't want Diana to be agitated.

964
00:56:05,529 --> 00:56:07,448
What if she wakes up
and sees you first thing?

965
00:56:07,823 --> 00:56:08,824
What do you need? Money?

966
00:56:08,908 --> 00:56:10,534
-Someone came to visit you.
-The Grim Reaper?

967
00:56:10,618 --> 00:56:11,994
-It's Patricia.
-Where is she?

968
00:56:12,078 --> 00:56:13,746
Can we stay here?

969
00:56:13,829 --> 00:56:15,372
We've got nowhere else to go.

970
00:56:15,456 --> 00:56:16,791
Patricia is still your daughter.

971
00:56:16,874 --> 00:56:18,459
You think she still sees me as her mom?

972
00:56:18,542 --> 00:56:19,919
You have to tell them the truth.

973
00:56:20,002 --> 00:56:21,295
And that should fix everything?

974
00:56:21,378 --> 00:56:23,964
People think they know your whole story.

975
00:56:24,048 --> 00:56:27,218
You're all alone now
because no one can stand you!

976
00:56:27,301 --> 00:56:29,053
-Please stop.
-Enough!
